  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-06-03T15:33:18.453Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This is something that has bothered me for a long time, and I haven't really seen anyone else request it. It feels like VRChat doesn't care about the fact that the radial menu color can't be changed at all.\n\n**What colors we can already change:**\n\n* Small Option Menu\n\n* Big Option Menu\n\n* Join/Leave breadcrumb message\n\n* Finger Tracking / Pinch UI\n\n* Nametags\n\nAll of these elements adapt to the color you set in the VRChat Plus color options. But the one thing that always stays in that ugly cyan color is the radial menu. It’s been like this for months now. How long will it take VRChat to realize this is a bad approach to monetizing a subscription? Why is everything else customizable except the radial menu?\n\nI've worked with Unity for years, and this is honestly one of the easiest things to make customizable. I’d even love to make a pull request if there was an actual GitHub. Please, for the sake of your community and the people who have supported you for years, add this as an option.",
